    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d288">

                <pb facs="0592" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v05p1/pg548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/12–1754: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Department of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret<lb/>priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1954-12-17T15:00:00+01:00">December 17,
                            1954—3 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Dulte 6. Eyes only Hoover for President. Am happy to advise that NATO
                    Ministerial Council has just unanimously approved Military Committee report for
                    purposes of planning and preparation with understanding that this approval did
                    not involve any delegation to <pb facs="0593" n="549" xml:id="pg549"/> military
                    of responsibility of governments for deciding on action in event of
                        hostilities.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d288-f1"/> Approving resolution was worked
                    out by us yesterday in conversations first with United Kingdom and Canada, then
                    with France.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d288-f2"/> It is entirely satisfactory to
                    Gruenther and Radford.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d288-f1" n="1" xml:id="d288-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram Secto 21, Dec. 18, from Paris, <ref target="#pg557">p.
